      "id": 1,
      "text": "Colonel Samuel Woods founded Woods Landing in 1883 as a saloon for lumberjacks, freighters, and stage drivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://woodslanding.com/about.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Woods Landing Dancehall features a unique floor supported by twenty-four boxcar springs to provide bounce and flexibility.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://woodslanding.com/about.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Woods Landing-Jelm is situated at the base of the Medicine Bow Mountains in the Big Laramie Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://woodslanding.com/about.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Dancehall in Woods Landing-Jelm was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1986.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://woodslanding.com/about.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mayme and Clarence Lewellen opened a filling station and sandwich stand in 1927 that became the General Country Store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
